        <p>WBRICLY CHAT.—Subject Second-hand Furniture.— The opening of Spring is the time for the busy house- wife to put her house in order, therefore the matter of furni- shing must be well discussrd. We cannot, therefore, do brtter than advise a visit to Worsley's before definitely de- ciding where and what to purchase. This visit cannot pos- sibly but prove remunerative, if only in experience. " The Pantheon " being a hive of industry, it is a palatial pile of buildings close to the Central Station, having a frontage ot nearly 150 feet This immense building is filled from floor to ceiling (six storeys) with the grandest collection of High- class Second-hand Furniture in the World. This is not an exaggeration, but can be verified by ocular demonstrat ion if you pay a visit to Manchester. Suites of Bedroom Furni- ture, for instance, by such makers as Goodall, Lamb, Ogden, &amp;C., original cost from £2OO to 2300, for from £5O to £7O ; suites, original cost £5O to £7O, for £lO to £2O. Pay a visit and see for younielf ; you can surely use your common sense, and see if Worsley's is the place as described.</p>
        <p>To COUNTRY BUYERS.—The enormous patronage en- joyed by Worsley's from customers all over Lancashire, Yorkshire, Cheshire, The Potteries. all over the North, The Midla.ids, and Wales, will prove how much is the saving effected by purch.sing at WOr a ley's. In future carriage will be paid on all orders over £2O to ally part of England and Wales. It is only fair to say that better value could not be obtained than Worts ey's New Goods and the Second-hand Furniture simply bewilders and demoralises competition. Never mind what • listance 3ou live from Manchester, it will pay you to visit Worsley's ; you will save quite 50 per cent.</p>
        <p>`triUTIoN —Beware of buying new London jerrybuilt fur- niture. no matter how low the price is— it Is dear at any price. Woreley's have second-hand reliable furniture by good makers, which will last for ages. There is no disputing the fact that high-claas second-hand fu, niture is better than new. The only fault is that sometimes the article is old- fashioned. This is easily remedied at Woreley's, they having over 50 cabinet makers at work modernising second-hand fur- niture when necessary. For instance, second-hand side- boards are easily modernised by having the baoks raised, the plates bevelled, and the panels carved. You never need fear cracking, blistering. gni,' eaten, or moth eaten furniture at Woreley's. Second-hand furniture is not troubled with these complaints. They give a written warranty tor 10 years with auk furniehhing orders.</p>
        <p>JEW FURNITURE All Worslev's new furniture is their own make. Of course it is obviously impossible to sup- ply every requiremant second-hard. Worsl-y's have, there- fore. erected a Cabinet Works in Cite-road, with an immense stock of set:oned imb,r for the production of reliable furni- ture. Every item in the Bedding Department is new, gu,ran- teed pure, under minute inspection.</p>
